border patrol officials tell fox news  that a majority of asylum seekers at the  southern border are being returned to  mexico now that's after the supreme  court ordered last month that the trump  era policy be reinstated jonathan hunt  is live in la jolla texas for us where  you can catch us up hi jonathan  hi dana we're trying to get official  word from either the department of  homeland security homeland security or  the white house as to whether there has  been a formal order since that supreme  court ruling sent down to border patrol  agents but as you look at pictures of  families arriving here in la jolla early  sunday evening i can tell you that at  least one border patrol supervisor is  telling us that now  all families are being sent back unless  they have a child  under the age of one pregnant women are  being allowed to stay as well but that  is about it according to this border  patrol officials others are all being  sent back to mexico in the wake of that  supreme court ruling now when they go  back to mexico they are often in the  camps that we have seen uh for many  months now just on the other side in  tijuana the camps you're looking at  right now for instance  under the what were called the migrant  protection protocols now this is causing  some blowback from immigration advocacy  groups a whole slew of them have sent a  letter to the mexican president saying  that he should stand up to the biden  administration if they do reinstate the  remain in mexico policy the letter says  in part quote as a sovereign nation  mexico has the right to reject the  reinstatement of mpp or any future  iteration with this policy that aims to  externalize the us border into mexican  territory it is impossible to  re-implement mpp in a way that upholds  human rights and due process and mexico  has the responsibility to block this  detrimental policy now it's too early to  say of course as apprehensions continue  right along the mexico border this video  you're looking at now in laredo texas  it's too early to say whether if indeed  those migrant families are being  returned in greater numbers to mexico  whether that will have an effect in  perhaps dissuading some to try crossing  the border illegally would you to get  new figures for august at least dana  from customs and border protection  probably around the end of this week  that will give us the total for the  number of encounters in august remember  in july we had a record 212 000  anecdotally i would say that we might be  slightly below that but we're only in  one area of the border obviously we  can't see the bigger picture uh but it's  going to be very interesting to see what  those august figures are dana well it  didn't really slow down in the hot  summer months as it usually does so  we'll look forward to getting those  numbers jonathan thank you
 

